.TH auto-passwd-user-expiration 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-passwd-user-expiration - Set password expiration for a user

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-passwd-user-expiration username expire-days [warning-days]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
username        The user whose password should expire
expire-days     Number of days before the password expires
warning-days    Number of days before expiration to warn the user
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-passwd-user-expiration
command sets an individual user's password expiration to
the number of days specified.  If a third argument is
provided, the user will receive a warning that many days
before password expiration.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-passwd-user-expiration
.ad
.fi

